{"kind":"report","text":"APPROVED for proposed-profile feasibility publication across all 39 exact artifacts of request 775 at clean 756bf4f9b28b5b42f85b4cd32814e7c83041050f, tree ee106c2037f3132d576b5463e1605ea81ac26833. Independent noseq-reviewer verdict under promise adae760ab530eab98d04ea3521e0ac5944279776. This approval resolves P1D-01/02 from review 734/54c581efb0211c3354e3624e4e0b7ecc767fe695. It does not adopt production cryptography, close G1–G5 or authorize P2–P9/deployment.\n\nI retained the full candidate review and G2-S01–S06 coverage recorded in 734, checked the fresh request and its three attachments against all 39 paths/head bindings, and independently reviewed all six changed files. No other source bytes changed from the previously reviewed candidate. Governing request 687, ratified direction 685/686, input audit 683 and the existing named-prefix/owner-attestation/custody boundaries still apply.\n\nP1D-01 resolved: closurePlan now retrieves and compares exact root, checkpoint, locator and every original order through its selected store, alongside the existing manifest/chunk verification. SEG-COMPLETE additionally requires the separately charged declaration to be confirmed and read back exactly before publishing complete T. Failure leaves the reserved preparation, charged inventory and prior complete frontier intact. The actual native suite exercises omitted and response-uncertain roots before and after intact reconstruction, an unconfirmed declaration, suppressed/substituted root/order/declaration bytes, unchanged charges and positive exact retry. These checks repair present eligibility behavior without claiming production fsync or transaction guarantees.\n\nP1D-02 resolved: suffixAvailable now compares selected T with the caller's original requested position, independent of selection's clamp to F. Actual socket offers distinguish equal T=F, requests beyond F with either null or exact checkpoint selection, an unsealed retained suffix, requests below the first eligible checkpoint and an unavailable exact newer checkpoint. The documentation defines the flag accordingly; it does not claim global freshness.\n\nI independently reran npm ci, npm run check, npm run build and the complete probe:segmented-recovery at this clean source. All 115 tests passed:102 mandatory prerequisites, six Node and six actual Chromium segmented cases, and the expanded real native composition, with preserved native size/COUNT observations. Run 479f865b-ad84-40b9-9ac3-dd9ecc603517/evidence.json SHA256 3ceafe751c3bbf6764d766bb37907bb6a5ca525faa738a46440bfa475d269769. Command logs are in artifacts/segmented-recovery/reviewer-fix-verification/a4343daa-536a-4f7b-a9b9-f8ee38b09abf. I used the existing unmodified native source 4cd3cf64850caf47dda46c2a2abbbf3525a64d10 and binary SHA256 028f26b98b0b895ed4d32f83642e3fa25173f3498330e9bfc2567a3fc06ffab4; no native/cache edits or rebuild occurred.\n\nA separate reviewer-authored real native regression repeats the original two failures on a fresh two-entry world: omitted root completion refuses, the same state reconstructed from disk still refuses, exact root upload/retry completes with the original 50,958-byte total charge, and requested3 at T=F=2 reports unavailable for both null and exact checkpoint selection. Requested2 reports available. Script, result, native configuration, signed objects, trace and raw report are retained in artifacts/segmented-recovery/reviewer-fix-experiments/66129200-ee93-4583-92f5-b4584d740595; result.json SHA256 20d7f6c88e6b4c29ef2cc5df0f844d045dea7649ad7190297962cc3141b42437.\n\nAll 44 independent public-verifier/gate outcomes matched: one valid current observation accepted, 39 malformed inputs rejected, and four correctly invoked gate/forged-approval cases rejected. This includes all 13 required-case omission, duplicate/skipped/failed cases, source/tree/lock/profile/library/native/prerequisite/schema changes, missing commands/observations, corrupt and rehashed raw reports, altered frontier/root/definition, skipped raw test, fake typecheck arguments, changed Welcome/signed delivery, omitted completion failure, refunded incomplete reservation and false beyond-F availability. Evidence: artifacts/segmented-recovery/reviewer-fix-negative/fcccd9c6-bb47-4aa4-8b8e-cb9b5056ac93/results.json (SHA256 1f0353f30a2351c2d484b358f4b97c3b049da734039dabcca42d81416a5815c5). These current corrected invocations include the stage argument and do not rely on the four mistaken reviewer gate invocations retained from the prior review.\n\nNo additional material issue emerged. The unchanged full coverage remains substantive: canonical acyclic segmented graph, exact original signed records and actual per-message openings, fresh independent history/grant keys, compact owner restoration and fourth-interval continuation, authentic newcomer Welcome, old-key/removed-holder crypto exclusion, bounded counts/encoded resources and conservative quota refusal, original v1 regressions and current-authority send/restore fences. The expanded result validator checks the required completion fault labels/unchanged charges and all frontier offer tuples. Documentation accurately preserves earlier failed records and the present scope.\n\nApproval is bounded: historical encrypted controls depend on the owner-attested context, old copied openings remain usable, a copied owner vault and immutable owner authority have the documented stronger capabilities, and named highest-retained-prefix service can expose older history after an unseen removal. The actual 16 MiB framing vector is not a semantic BodyCore, 65,536-key encoding is not a jointly admitted worst-case history, and small configured byte/quota tests do not establish a physical 256 MiB fill, 10,000-entry benchmark, deployment isolation, crash durability, production outbox or complete app runtime. All G1–G5 remain explicitly unpassed. Separate reviewed decisions, explicit root adoption and the separately commissioned detached-decision activation validator remain required. This verdict allows requester inspection/ratification and guarded publication of the exact candidate only. No source edits, merge, push, deployment or adoption were performed by this reviewer.","body":{"artifact":"git:sha1:77aeeeb3fa42aeb6babdf961f6397ba73fada68b#git:sha1:00d18d1ef659ed69ced7e1d8a94cb3af283a9017","head":"756bf4f9b28b5b42f85b4cd32814e7c83041050f","head_news_acknowledged":"[\"git:sha1:77aeeeb3fa42aeb6babdf961f6397ba73fada68b#git:sha1:adae760ab530eab98d04ea3521e0ac5944279776\"]","review_frontier":"git:sha1:77aeeeb3fa42aeb6babdf961f6397ba73fada68b#git:sha1:adae760ab530eab98d04ea3521e0ac5944279776","review_path":"reviewguard@1","verdict":"approved"}}